{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"Clean reproduction, 2026-09-XX session 6a3fecbb (claiming b939-bc68-1cb2-4ee9).\n\nMCP `claim_ticket` refused with \"the local ticket store is 2 commit(s) BEHIND the shared store\". Checked the store directly in /Users/joeoakhart/rebar/.tickets-tracker: branch `tickets`, `git fetch origin tickets`, then `git rev-list --left-right --count HEAD...origin/tickets` reported **0 0** — the clone was current, not behind. Retried the MCP claim anyway: same refusal.\n\nThe identical claim through the local CLI succeeded immediately:\n\n    rebar claim b939-bc68-1cb2-4ee9\n    claimed b939-bc68-1cb2-4ee9: open -> in_progress (assignee joeoakhart@navapbc.com)\n\nIndependent confirmation that the stale view lives in the MCP process, not the store: after that successful claim, MCP `show_ticket` still reported b939 as `status: \"open\"`.\n\nSo the staleness check is reading a cached snapshot rather than the on-disk store, and it is **hard-blocking writes** on the strength of that cache — a false refusal, not a warning.\n\nRecovery pattern that worked, worth documenting wherever this is fixed: when an MCP tracker op refuses on staleness, verify the store with read-only raw git first, and if it is current, run the op through the local CLI."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793441281672116001,"uuid":"dcaf50f7-fb1a-4bae-b495-4a5e4ab8faeb"}